# Client-Side Supabase Patterns

## Client Setup

### Server-Side Config (Astro Frontmatter)
```typescript
import { supabaseUrl, supabaseAnonKey } from '../utils/supabase';

// Get Supabase config to pass to client - SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH
const supabaseConfig = {
  url: supabaseUrl,
  anonKey: supabaseAnonKey
};
```

### Client-Side Setup (Browser Only)
```javascript
// In inline script with define:vars
<script is:inline define:vars={{ supabaseConfig }}>
  // Get config passed from server-side - NO HARDCODED VALUES
  const supabaseUrl = supabaseConfig.url;
  const supabaseAnonKey = supabaseConfig.anonKey;
  
  // Create client in browser
  const supabase = window.supabase.createClient(supabaseUrl, supabaseAnonKey);
</script>
```

## Server-Side Data Fetching (Astro)
```typescript
// In .astro frontmatter
const { data: articles, error } = await supabase
  .from('test_articles')
  .select('*')
  .order('created_at', { ascending: false });

// Fetch aggregated data
const { data: likeCounts } = await supabase
  .from('article_like_counts')
  .select('*');

// Combine data
const articlesWithLikes = articles?.map(article => ({
  ...article,
  like_count: likeCounts?.find(lc => lc.article_id === article.id)?.like_count || 0
})) || [];
```

## Critical Rule: Authentication is Browser-Side Only

**NEVER** do authentication on the server-side. All auth operations must happen in the browser:
- `supabase.auth.signInAnonymously()` - Browser only
- `supabase.auth.getUser()` - Browser only  
- All auth state management - Browser only

### Proper Config Passing Pattern
```astro
---
// Server-side: Get config from single source
import { supabaseUrl, supabaseAnonKey } from '../utils/supabase';

const supabaseConfig = {
  url: supabaseUrl,
  anonKey: supabaseAnonKey
};
---

<script is:inline define:vars={{ supabaseConfig }}>
  // Client-side: Use passed config - NO HARDCODED VALUES
  const supabaseUrl = supabaseConfig.url;
  const supabaseAnonKey = supabaseConfig.anonKey;
  
  // Load Supabase from CDN
  const script = document.createElement('script');
  script.src = 'https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@supabase/supabase-js@2/dist/umd/supabase.js';
  script.onload = initializeApp;
  document.head.appendChild(script);
  
  function initializeApp() {
    const supabase = window.supabase.createClient(supabaseUrl, supabaseAnonKey);
    // All auth operations happen here in browser
  }
</script>
```

## Anonymous User Operations

### Like/Unlike Pattern
```javascript
// Check existing likes for user
const { data } = await supabase
  .from('article_likes')
  .select('article_id')
  .eq('user_fingerprint', userFingerprint);

// Insert like
const { error } = await supabase
  .from('article_likes')
  .insert({
    article_id: articleId,
    user_fingerprint: userFingerprint
  });

// Remove like
const { error } = await supabase
  .from('article_likes')
  .delete()
  .eq('article_id', articleId)
  .eq('user_fingerprint', userFingerprint);
```

### State Management
```javascript
// Track liked articles locally
const likedArticles = new Set();

// Update UI immediately
if (!error) {
  likedArticles.add(articleId);
  button.classList.add('liked', 'text-red-600', 'bg-red-50');
  heartIcon.setAttribute('fill', 'currentColor');
  likeCountSpan.textContent = parseInt(likeCountSpan.textContent) + 1;
}
```

## Error Handling Patterns

### Silent Error Handling
```javascript
try {
  // Database operation
} catch (error) {
  // Silent error handling for likes
  // Don't show errors to users for non-critical features
}
```

### Auth Error Handling
```javascript
const { error: authError } = await supabase.auth.signInAnonymously();

if (authError) {
  signingIn = false;
  return false; // Fail gracefully
}
```

## LocalStorage Integration
```javascript
// Track user voting history
localStorage.setItem('supabase_has_voted', 'true');

// Auto-authenticate returning voters
const hasVotedBefore = localStorage.getItem('supabase_has_voted') === 'true';
if (hasVotedBefore && !isSignedIn) {
  await ensureSignedIn();
}
```

## Event Handling
```javascript
// Setup event listeners after DOM ready
function setupEventListeners() {
  const likeButtons = document.querySelectorAll('.like-btn');
  
  likeButtons.forEach((button) => {
    button.addEventListener('click', async (e) => {
      e.preventDefault();
      e.stopPropagation();
      const articleId = parseInt(button.dataset.articleId);
      await handleLike(articleId);
    });
  });
}

// Handle DOM ready state
if (document.readyState === 'loading') {
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', setupEventListeners);
} else {
  setupEventListeners();
}
```

